# Security & Deployment Rules

## Environment Variables — Backend
```bash
# Server
APP_ENV=production          # development | staging | production
APP_PORT=8080
APP_SECRET_KEY=             # 32+ byte random hex — NEVER commit

# Database
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
DATABASE_MAX_OPEN_CONNS=25
DATABASE_MAX_IDLE_CONNS=5

# Redis
REDIS_URL=redis://:password@host:6379/0

# JWT
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=          # 32+ byte random — different from APP_SECRET_KEY
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=         # 32+ byte random — different from above
JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRY=15m
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRY=7d

# Admin seed
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=             # Strong password, set at deploy time

# Media
MEDIA_STORAGE_PATH=./uploads
MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://yourdomain.com/media
MEDIA_MAX_SIZE_MB=5

# CORS
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com

# Rate limiting
RATE_LIMIT_AUTH_RPM=5       # requests per minute per IP on auth endpoints
```

## JWT Rules
- Access token TTL: 15 minutes
- Refresh token TTL: 7 days, stored as HTTP-only cookie OR in Redis with JTI
- Include in payload: `sub` (user_id), `role`, `jti` (unique ID for revocation), `exp`, `iat`
- Refresh tokens stored in Redis — can be revoked instantly on logout
- On password change or account suspension: revoke all refresh tokens for that user
```go
type Claims struct {
    jwt.RegisteredClaims
    UserID string   `json:"sub"`
    Role   string   `json:"role"`
    JTI    string   `json:"jti"`
}
```

## Password Hashing
- Use `bcrypt` with cost factor 12 (minimum 10)
- Never log, serialize, or expose password hashes
- Compare using `bcrypt.CompareHashAndPassword` — constant-time
```go
hash, err := bcrypt.GenerateFromPassword([]byte(password), 12)
```

## Input Validation Rules
- ALL handler inputs validated via `go-playground/validator`
- Sanitize free-text fields: strip control characters, limit lengths
- File uploads: validate MIME type from file header bytes (not extension)
- URL params: validate UUID format before hitting DB
```go
func validateUUID(id string) (uuid.UUID, error) {
    parsed, err := uuid.Parse(id)
    if err != nil {
        return uuid.Nil, fiber.NewError(fiber.StatusBadRequest, "invalid id format")
    }
    return parsed, nil
}
```

## SQL Injection Prevention
- ALWAYS use GORM parameterized queries
- NEVER use string concatenation to build SQL
- NEVER use `db.Raw()` with user-supplied values without `?` placeholders
```go
// BAD
db.Raw("SELECT * FROM events WHERE title = '" + title + "'")

// GOOD
db.Raw("SELECT * FROM events WHERE title = ?", title)
// Or better — use GORM methods
db.Where("title ILIKE ?", "%"+title+"%").Find(&events)
```

## XSS / Content Security
- Backend: set security headers via Fiber Helmet middleware
```go
app.Use(helmet.New(helmet.Config{
    ContentSecurityPolicy: "default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'",
    XFrameOptions: "DENY",
    XContentTypeOptions: "nosniff",
    ReferrerPolicy: "strict-origin-when-cross-origin",
}))
```
- Frontend: Angular's template binding auto-escapes; never use `[innerHTML]` with user data; use `DomSanitizer.sanitize()` if absolutely necessary

## Rate Limiting
```go
// Auth endpoints only — use Redis sliding window
app.Post("/api/v1/auth/login", rateLimitMiddleware(5, time.Minute), handler.Login)
app.Post("/api/v1/auth/register", rateLimitMiddleware(3, time.Minute), handler.Register)
```

## HTTPS / TLS
- Production: TLS terminated at reverse proxy (nginx / Caddy)
- Never run Go server with plain HTTP in production
- HSTS header: `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`
- Frontend: Angular `HttpClient` configured to never downgrade to HTTP

## Docker Setup
```dockerfile
# backend/Dockerfile
FROM golang:1.22-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY go.mod go.sum ./
RUN go mod download
COPY . .
RUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux go build -ldflags="-s -w" -o server ./cmd/server

FROM scratch
COPY --from=builder /app/server /server
COPY --from=builder /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt /etc/ssl/certs/
EXPOSE 8080
ENTRYPOINT ["/server"]
```

```dockerfile
# frontend/Dockerfile
FROM oven/bun:1 AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json bun.lockb ./
RUN bun install --frozen-lockfile
COPY . .
RUN bun run build

FROM nginx:alpine
COPY --from=builder /app/dist/frontend/browser /usr/share/nginx/html
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
EXPOSE 80
```

## Logging & Observability
- Structured JSON logs in production (`zap` production config)
- Log levels: DEBUG (dev only), INFO (request/response summary), WARN (recoverable errors), ERROR (unexpected failures)
- Never log: passwords, JWT tokens, full request bodies with PII
- Request ID: generate UUID per request, attach to logger context, return as `X-Request-ID` header
- Health check endpoint: `GET /health` returns `{ "status": "ok", "db": "ok", "redis": "ok" }`

## Git / CI Rules
- `.env` files NEVER committed — `.gitignore` enforced
- Pre-commit hooks: `golangci-lint` for Go, `eslint` + `tsc --noEmit` for Angular
- PR requires: passing tests + lint + no secrets detected (use `gitleaks`)
- Dependency audit: `go mod tidy && govulncheck ./...` in CI pipeline
